1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:03,279
This is my bedroom in Istanbul.

2
00:00:03,279 --> 00:00:07,252
RiskLens found this wardrobe with
suitcases on top.

3
00:00:07,252 --> 00:00:13,210
It can't see if it's fixed to the wall, so
it asks

4
00:00:13,210 --> 00:00:14,700
you to check.

5
00:00:15,300 --> 00:00:17,397
I live in Istanbul.

6
00:00:17,397 --> 00:00:23,689
Here, getting ready for an earthquake also
means looking at what is

7
00:00:23,689 --> 00:00:25,262
inside our homes.

8
00:00:25,262 --> 00:00:31,554
Film one room for less than a minute, or
upload a video.

9
00:00:31,554 --> 00:00:34,700
Or open one of four examples.

10
00:00:35,300 --> 00:00:37,962
This is a live run.

11
00:00:37,962 --> 00:00:40,092
We shortened the waiting.

12
00:00:40,092 --> 00:00:46,481
First, Muse Spark looks at some frames and
decides which objects matter

13
00:00:46,481 --> 00:00:48,078
in this room.

14
00:00:48,078 --> 00:00:53,403
Then SAM 3.1 follows each object through
the whole video.

15
00:00:53,403 --> 00:00:59,792
So every finding points to a real frame
and a real box.

16
00:00:59,792 --> 00:01:03,519
Then Spark looks at the marked frames.

17
00:01:03,519 --> 00:01:08,843
It separates what it can see from what
needs checking.

18
00:01:08,843 --> 00:01:14,700
Last, it reads FEMA E-74 guidance to write
the next steps.

19
00:01:15,300 --> 00:01:22,356
Every finding shows what the video shows,
and what is still unknown.

20
00:01:22,356 --> 00:01:29,412
Each next step links to the FEMA section
the model really read.

21
00:01:29,412 --> 00:01:34,116
If that check fails, we show no steps.

22
00:01:34,116 --> 00:01:41,172
Muse Image can draw what a fix could look
like, but it

23
00:01:41,172 --> 00:01:44,700
doesn't prove your room is safe.

24
00:01:45,300 --> 00:01:51,041
After a fix, you film the item again.

25
00:01:51,041 --> 00:01:59,653
The same video cannot prove a change, and
RiskLens checks that before

26
00:01:59,653 --> 00:02:01,806
any model runs.

27
00:02:01,806 --> 00:02:09,700
A real change needs the same object and a
visible difference.

28
00:02:10,300 --> 00:02:17,049
I made three test rooms with Muse Image,
with hazards placed on purpose.

29
00:02:17,049 --> 00:02:19,126
Spark checked every view.

30
00:02:19,126 --> 00:02:25,355
RiskLens found five of five, four of four,
and four of five.

31
00:02:25,355 --> 00:02:30,547
It missed boxes that narrow the way to the
door.

32
00:02:30,547 --> 00:02:34,700
This is a test, not an accuracy claim.

33
00:02:35,300 --> 00:02:40,289
RiskLens is a visual check, not a building
inspection.

34
00:02:40,289 --> 00:02:46,940
It shows the evidence, it's honest about
what it can't see, and

35
00:02:46,940 --> 00:02:51,929
it helps you decide what to look at next.

36
00:02:51,929 --> 00:02:54,700
One room at a time.
